ns his head toward the small motionless Kael far in the RIGHT background under the white light. Hold that unreachable distance for the final beat to connect to the next wide shot. Real-time swift swordwork, no slow motion, no prolonged sword lock. Detailed painted cinematic materials, coherent faces and anatomy, readable separate blades, continuous hall, crisp blue and violet lighting. Natural sound only: two sword clashes, shield impact, armor movement, one sharp teleport crack and its soft hall echo. No speech, music, captions, subtitles, logos, blood, new characters, duplicates, extra arms, changed weapons or camera cut."
